% You are an expert TypeScript engineer. Implement `research_snapshot_selector`: select the read snapshot for one site without mutating snapshot history.

<include>prompts/context/sitevelocity-preamble.prompt</include>
<include>prompts/context/evidence_domain_types.prompt</include>

<pdd-reason>Selects the latest trustworthy Research Snapshot for reads, with explicit partial fallback and visible staleness.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[
  {"name":"selectResearchSnapshot","signature":"(input: SnapshotSelectionInput) -> SnapshotSelectionResult","returns":"SnapshotSelectionResult"}]}}
</pdd-interface>

<responsibility>
Choose exactly one snapshot manifest (or none) to serve reads for one site, from immutable snapshot history, an explicit partial policy, a freshness policy, and a read timestamp.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
- DOES NOT create, refresh, repair, merge, or delete snapshots or their contents.
- DOES NOT load or validate the findings, evidence, or events a snapshot references.
- DOES NOT define partial or freshness policy; it applies only the supplied policies.
- DOES NOT schedule refreshes or decide whether a refresh should run.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
- Blank: a string that is empty or contains only whitespace.
- Valid manifest: non-blank `id` and `siteId`; `createdAt` and `sourceCutoff` parse as ISO 8601 timestamps with `sourceCutoff` <= `createdAt`; `runIds` non-empty with no blank entry; category names non-blank and unique; `status` one of the declared statuses; and a `complete` manifest has every category entry with status `complete`.
- Invalid: a manifest that fails any valid-manifest condition.
- Matching manifest: a valid manifest whose `siteId` equals the input `siteId`.
- Eligible complete snapshot: a matching manifest with status `complete`.
- Eligible partial snapshot: a matching manifest with status `partial`, where `partialPolicy.allowPartial` is true, every category in `partialPolicy.requiredCategories` has status `complete`, and the count of non-`complete` category entries is at most `partialPolicy.maxMissingCategories`. A partial manifest failing any of these is incomplete beyond policy.
- Recency order: greater `sourceCutoff` first (compared as epoch milliseconds), then greater `createdAt`, then greater `id` by code-unit order. Latest = first in recency order. This is the approved deterministic tie-breaker.
- Effective category date: the category entry's `sourceDate`, or the manifest's `sourceCutoff` when `sourceDate` is null.
- Stale category: a category whose effective date is more than its max age in days before `readAt`; max age is `freshnessPolicy.maxAgeDaysByCategory[category]`, falling back to `defaultMaxAgeDays`; a null fallback means never stale.
- Missing categories: category entries with status `missing` or `failed`.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Select the latest eligible complete snapshot with reason code `latest_complete` whenever at least one exists, even when a partial, failed, or invalid manifest precedes it in the recency order.
R2 (MUST): Select the latest eligible partial snapshot with reason code `partial_fallback` only when no eligible complete snapshot exists.
R3 (MUST): Never select a manifest that is failed, rejected, invalid, non-matching, or incomplete beyond policy.
R4 (MUST): Return the same selection whether or not the input additionally contains manifests excluded by R3 — a newer failed refresh never displaces the previously selectable valid snapshot.
R5 (MUST): Report the selected snapshot's ID, status, `sourceCutoff`, `createdAt`, `runIds`, stale categories, and missing categories exactly as derived from that one manifest and the freshness policy, never hiding staleness.

R6 (MUST): Order candidates only by the recency order, resolving equal timestamps with its declared tie-breaker; derive every field of the result from the single selected manifest and never merge fields across manifests; and, for every input matching the declared shape, produce identical output for structurally identical input, never mutate the input, and never throw.

R7 (MUST): Return `selection: "none"` with reason code `no_snapshots` when the manifest list is empty, and `no_eligible_snapshot` when manifests exist but none is eligible.
</contract_rules>

<interface_types>

The shared types `SnapshotStatus`, `SnapshotCategoryStatus`, and `SnapshotManifest` are declared in the included evidence-domain types and are frozen. This module additionally declares:

```ts
interface PartialPolicy {
  allowPartial: boolean;
  requiredCategories: string[];
  maxMissingCategories: number;
}

interface FreshnessPolicy {
  maxAgeDaysByCategory: { [category: string]: number };
  defaultMaxAgeDays: number | null; // null = never stale by default
}

interface SnapshotSelectionInput {
  siteId: string;
  manifests: SnapshotManifest[];
  partialPolicy: PartialPolicy;
  freshnessPolicy: FreshnessPolicy;
  readAt: string; // ISO 8601
}

type SelectedReasonCode = "latest_complete" | "partial_fallback";
type NoneReasonCode = "no_snapshots" | "no_eligible_snapshot";

interface SelectedSnapshot {
  selection: "complete" | "partial"; // mirrors the selected manifest's status
  snapshotId: string;
  status: "complete" | "partial";
  sourceCutoff: string;
  createdAt: string;
  runIds: string[];
  staleCategories: string[];   // stale category names, in the manifest's category order
  missingCategories: string[]; // missing/failed category names, in the manifest's category order
  reasonCode: SelectedReasonCode;
}

interface NoSnapshot {
  selection: "none";
  reasonCode: NoneReasonCode;
}

type SnapshotSelectionResult = SelectedSnapshot | NoSnapshot;
```

Export exactly one public function:

```ts
export function selectResearchSnapshot(input: SnapshotSelectionInput): SnapshotSelectionResult;
```

</interface_types>

